:name: RESTS STM32F429 UART bridge
:description: Loads the RESTS Debug ELF on an STM32F429ZITx and exposes sysbus.usart1 as a TCP socket terminal on 127.0.0.1:12345 for the host_app client.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The '@' prefix makes Renode resolve the path against its working directory;
# a plain relative string ("./Debug/...") is rejected by LoadELF. Run Renode
# from the repository root (launch_renode.ps1 does this) or override $elf with
# an absolute path: $elf?=@D:/path/to/RESTS_STM32.elf
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
$elf?=@./Debug/RESTS_STM32.elf
$port?=12345

using sysbus

mach create "rests-f429"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/stm32f429.repl
sysbus LoadELF $elf

# Expose the emulated USART1 as a TCP server. host_app connects to
# 127.0.0.1:12345 and speaks the RESTS protocol (HELLO?, LANG:.., PTT:*).
# NOTE: Renode binds this to all interfaces (0.0.0.0), not just loopback.
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $port "term" false
connector Connect sysbus.usart1 term

# Useful while debugging the protocol:
# showAnalyzer usart1

start
